	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "State of California's Department of Business Oversight" ;
	<https://www.omg.org/spec/Commons/AnnotationVocabulary/explanatoryNote> "The Department of Business Oversight (DBO) protects consumers and oversees financial service providers and products. The DBO supervises the operations of state-licensed financial institutions, including banks, credit unions and money transmitters. Additionally, the DBO licenses and regulates a variety of financial service providers, including securities brokers and dealers, investment advisers, payday lenders and other consumer finance lenders." ;
