	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Office of the Comptroller of the Currency" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "OCC, which charters, regulates, and supervises all national banks and federal savings associations as well as federal branches and agencies of foreign banks. The OCC is an independent bureau of the U.S. Department of the Treasury." ;
	<https://www.omg.org/spec/Commons/AnnotationVocabulary/abbreviation> "OCC" ;
	<https://www.omg.org/spec/Commons/AnnotationVocabulary/explanatoryNote> "The mission of the OCC is to ensure that national banks and federal savings associations operate in a safe and sound manner, provide fair access to financial services, treat customers fairly, and comply with applicable laws and regulations." ;
