	<https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/FND/Accounting/CurrencyAmount/hasNumericCode> "940" ;
	<https://www.omg.org/spec/Commons/AnnotationVocabulary/explanatoryNote> "The UYI (URUIURUI) is used for issuance of debt instruments by the Uruguayan government in the international global bond market. It is calculated based on an established methodology using underlying inflationary statistics in the Uruguayan market. (Introduced in 2002)." ;
	<https://www.omg.org/spec/Commons/ContextualDesignators/isUsedBy> <https://www.omg.org/spec/LCC/Countries/ISO3166-1-CountryCodes/Uruguay> ;
