	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://www.omg.org/spec/LCC/Countries/CountryRepresentation/> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has numeric region code" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "a three-digit numeric code assigned to a region according to some code set" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "For certain territories that do not have an alternate designation (i.e. country or country subdivision code in ISO 3166), the corresponding numeric code may have four digits." .
<https://www.omg.org/spec/LCC/Countries/CountryRepresentation/hasPart> <http://www.omg.org/techprocess/ab/SpecificationMetadata/directSource> "Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy at http://plato.stanford.edu/entries/mereology/" ;
	a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://www.omg.org/spec/LCC/Countries/CountryRepresentation/> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has part" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "indicates any portion of something, regardless of whether the portion itself is attached to the remainder or detached; cognitively salient or arbitrarily demarcated; self-connected or disconnected; homogeneous or gerrymandered; material or immaterial; extended or unextended; spatial or temporal" .
<https://www.omg.org/spec/LCC/Countries/CountryRepresentation/hasRemarks> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.omg.org/spec/LCC/Countries/CountryRepresentation/GeopoliticalEntity> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://www.omg.org/spec/LCC/Countries/CountryRepresentation/> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has remarks" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "remarks, such as other widely-used country names, names of geographically separated territories covered by the coding system, and so forth" .
<https://www.omg.org/spec/LCC/Countries/CountryRepresentation/hasSubregion> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.omg.org/spec/LCC/Countries/CountryRepresentation/GeographicRegion> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://www.omg.org/spec/LCC/Countries/CountryRepresentation/> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has subregion" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://www.omg.org/spec/LCC/Countries/CountryRepresentation/GeographicRegion> ;
